WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
[moody, intense intro music plays]

01:09.652 --> 01:11.154
[mysterious music playing]

01:14.449 --> 01:15.825
[shutter snapping]

01:20.955 --> 01:22.165
Ooh! Oh!

01:23.666 --> 01:24.667
Wait! Oh!

01:26.127 --> 01:27.587
Oh God.

01:39.557 --> 01:40.558
[music trails off]

01:42.560 --> 01:44.562
[engine turns over]

01:52.946 --> 01:54.364
Wow, that sunset.

01:54.447 --> 01:56.324
[gentle music playing]

01:56.407 --> 01:57.408
Incredible.

02:37.866 --> 02:40.160
Did you buy that
with the money you won from me?

02:41.995 --> 02:43.913
No. I got this with my own money.

02:44.956 --> 02:46.207
You want one?

02:48.543 --> 02:49.544
[exhales]

02:51.963 --> 02:53.965
Is that the only gambling you do?

02:55.466 --> 02:58.178
One time,
I bet my whole life on something.

02:58.970 --> 02:59.804
Did you win?

03:01.306 --> 03:02.223
I plan to.

03:07.562 --> 03:10.732
Do you live near here?
I saw you playing at the Go house.

03:10.815 --> 03:12.358
I guess you live around here.

03:12.942 --> 03:14.194
I'm close, so…

03:15.069 --> 03:15.904
Do you work nearby?

03:16.696 --> 03:19.782
Why aren't you eating?
Don't eat food from convenience stores?

03:19.866 --> 03:22.202
Can't say I do. Watching my carbs.

03:26.873 --> 03:28.541
You don't like to share much, do you?

03:28.625 --> 03:30.543
Do you usually ask so many things?

03:30.627 --> 03:34.923
Normally, I keep quiet, believe it or not.

03:35.006 --> 03:36.007
[chuckles]

03:41.804 --> 03:43.306
Why do you like to play Go?

03:45.975 --> 03:49.979
I like it because you engage
in an intense battle in silence.

03:51.648 --> 03:56.736
And also, I like that you get to destroy
somebody's house in order to win.

04:05.995 --> 04:07.997
[tense, mysterious music playing]

04:14.545 --> 04:16.631
Why don't we play together sometime?

04:18.633 --> 04:20.593
Since I now know what you like.

04:22.762 --> 04:24.514
JAEPYEONG CONSTRUCTION
CEO HA DO-YEONG

04:24.597 --> 04:25.598
I'm Ha Do-yeong.

04:29.644 --> 04:32.146
Next time,
bring some more money when we play.

04:33.106 --> 04:34.440
You won't eat this, right?

04:40.738 --> 04:41.948
[shutter snapping]

04:44.492 --> 04:45.410
[music trails off]

05:01.134 --> 05:03.052
Is that supposed to be your breakfast?

05:06.180 --> 05:07.932
You come here every morning, huh?

05:08.933 --> 05:10.727
Do you ever cook for yourself?

05:12.312 --> 05:14.147
[Dong-eun] Did you have
your breakfast already?

05:16.691 --> 05:18.985
Semyeong Elementary,
is that where you work?

05:19.068 --> 05:20.945
I noticed the sticker on your car.

05:21.029 --> 05:22.697
That's a great job to have.

05:28.828 --> 05:30.747
Can I ask you about something as well?

05:32.332 --> 05:34.751
You're the owner
of Semyeong Real Estate, right?

05:34.834 --> 05:38.671
I think you were the one I ran into
when I first looked for a place.

05:39.797 --> 05:40.965
Yeah, that was me.

05:41.549 --> 05:43.634
Ever since I moved in here,

05:44.677 --> 05:47.180
I noticed that my rent's
less than anyone else's around.

05:48.389 --> 05:49.515
Why did you do that?

05:50.266 --> 05:52.602
It's a good thing when the rent's so low.

05:53.311 --> 05:55.271
A teacher doesn't make much these days.

05:56.939 --> 05:59.525
But you couldn't have known
that I was a teacher.

06:05.865 --> 06:07.408
I'm sorry for asking here,

06:08.618 --> 06:12.580
but is it 'cause the condo's haunted?

06:13.915 --> 06:14.749
Huh?

06:15.249 --> 06:17.251
[hearty laughter]

06:18.961 --> 06:21.714
I was thinking you had
absolutely no sense of humor.

06:21.798 --> 06:22.799
That's rich.

06:23.633 --> 06:25.760
Make sure that you take
your trash with you

06:25.843 --> 06:27.220
when you head back down.

06:29.013 --> 06:31.015
[gentle acoustic guitar music playing]

06:33.267 --> 06:36.229
[Hyeon-nam] Here are
my receipts, parking, gas,

06:36.312 --> 06:38.356
and everything else
I needed for our operation.

06:38.439 --> 06:39.524
I'm sorry.

06:39.607 --> 06:41.567
Seems like revenge is pretty expensive.

06:43.403 --> 06:45.279
[singer singing in Korean]

06:47.615 --> 06:48.533
MONTHLY PARKING FEE

06:48.616 --> 06:51.077
-GAS MONEY
-OTHER EXPENSES

06:51.160 --> 06:54.914
[Dong-eun] I spent my twenties tutoring
so I could pay for things like this.

06:55.415 --> 06:57.917
I've got plenty saved up, so don't worry.

07:07.176 --> 07:08.553
[Hyeon-nam] After following them,

07:08.636 --> 07:10.930
I found Hye-jeong is
the easiest to predict.

07:11.013 --> 07:12.432
She's always on her phone.

07:12.932 --> 07:15.518
I've been thinking
I should try and steal her phone.

07:16.185 --> 07:17.854
I think I can be pretty talented.

07:18.896 --> 07:20.731
-[scribbling forcefully]
-[silently mouthing]

07:27.447 --> 07:29.157
I THINK I'M PRETTY TALENTED

07:30.241 --> 07:31.701
[fond chuckle]

07:31.784 --> 07:33.244
[Dong-eun] Could you do that?

07:34.203 --> 07:35.538
[Hyeon-nam] Just leave it to me.

07:36.122 --> 07:38.791
By the way, did you meet
Park Yeon-jin in person yet?

07:38.875 --> 07:40.460
Everything went smooth, right?

07:43.463 --> 07:45.006
[chuckles]

07:47.216 --> 07:48.468
[Dong-eun] Do you want to meet?

07:50.845 --> 07:51.762
[song trails off]

07:52.472 --> 07:54.640
[Hyeon-nam] Were you scared? Intimidated?

07:54.724 --> 07:57.727
You should have stomped on her soul
like she was nothing but a piece of paper.

07:59.979 --> 08:01.397
I did one of those things.

08:01.481 --> 08:03.691
[sighs] That's good. I'm glad.

08:04.358 --> 08:06.110
That's really good. Great job.

08:06.861 --> 08:08.654
I was so worried about you.

08:09.614 --> 08:10.615
Oh!

08:12.158 --> 08:13.910
Remember Park Yeon-jin's mom?

08:14.577 --> 08:16.454
Oh, the photo came out blurry.

08:17.163 --> 08:20.416
She visited that shaman again,
two weeks after her last visit.

08:20.500 --> 08:21.667
With the same man, too.

08:21.751 --> 08:25.588
I thought they might be dating,
but they leave in separate cars.

08:25.671 --> 08:27.215
They even arrive separately.

08:27.298 --> 08:30.134
If there's a pattern here,
there must be a reason.

08:30.718 --> 08:33.095
-Let me know if you find anything else.
-Uh-huh.

08:34.013 --> 08:37.934
And did you happen to tail this person?

08:39.477 --> 08:40.478
What do you mean by tail?

08:41.103 --> 08:42.522
Just don't try to follow this man.

08:43.314 --> 08:45.942
I didn't want to scare you
so I didn't tell you this,

08:46.025 --> 08:47.026
but he's a cop.

08:48.236 --> 08:50.947
When we first met, he was the chief.
Maybe he moved up.

08:51.030 --> 08:53.574
He's the senior
superintendent-general at Bukbu.

08:53.658 --> 08:56.869
He's fallen behind most of his classmates
who are all chiefs now.

08:57.578 --> 08:58.913
How did you know that?

08:59.413 --> 09:01.874
Didn't you see the receipts
for that soup restaurant?

09:01.958 --> 09:04.335
I found four soup restaurants
near the police station,

09:04.418 --> 09:06.170
and just waited for him. [chuckles]

09:08.297 --> 09:10.341
When you threatened me
the first time we met…

09:12.426 --> 09:15.012
I had no idea how scary you really are.

09:15.972 --> 09:17.056
Me?

09:17.139 --> 09:18.933
[hearty laughter]

09:24.438 --> 09:25.606
Don't put yourself at risk.

09:29.235 --> 09:30.236
Yeah, I won't.

09:30.319 --> 09:33.906
Oh, and can you look here for me?
Think of this as part of the job.

09:33.990 --> 09:34.907
Hang on, I don't--

09:34.991 --> 09:36.117
[shutter snap echoing]

09:36.200 --> 09:37.952
[tense music playing]

09:42.748 --> 09:44.709
[tense music intensifying]

09:44.792 --> 09:45.918
[music stops abruptly]

09:47.169 --> 09:50.047
[Hyeon-nam] What?
Is something wrong? Are you okay?

09:51.257 --> 09:52.258
I'm… I'm so sorry.

09:53.259 --> 09:54.343
Oh…

09:54.427 --> 09:56.596
I'm good at pictures of flowers and birds.

09:57.096 --> 09:59.974
But when I take photos of people,
my hands start to shake.

10:04.103 --> 10:06.689
[Dong-eun breathing shakily]

10:06.772 --> 10:07.857
It's okay now.

10:09.150 --> 10:11.027
[gentle Korean pop ballad playing]

10:12.028 --> 10:12.945
Take another.

10:25.374 --> 10:26.959
I wanna try one more.

10:42.892 --> 10:43.893
[song trails off]

11:00.660 --> 11:02.953
My, oh, my. [woman laughs]

11:03.037 --> 11:05.289
Ye-sol, sweetie,
it's your first Gucci, huh?

11:06.123 --> 11:09.168
Do you like what Grandma got you? Hmm?

11:09.251 --> 11:11.587
"Babies can't tell the difference."

11:11.671 --> 11:13.964
"Why get Gucci
when she won't be wearing it in a month?

11:14.632 --> 11:15.716
Is that right?

11:17.551 --> 11:19.762
-Yes?
-You know, you reap what you sow.

11:20.721 --> 11:23.808
You only live the way you do,
because of the way you think.

11:24.558 --> 11:26.977
-Go get a new nanny.
-Sure.

11:28.187 --> 11:31.649
Everything I owe you will be
deposited directly into your account.

11:31.732 --> 11:33.484
-[disappointed grunt]
-Thanks for your work.

11:35.361 --> 11:36.946
[nanny sighs] Screw this.

11:41.158 --> 11:44.829
Hold onto her newborn clothes
so she has it for any important event.

11:44.912 --> 11:48.165
Like when you had her,
you'll need to try your hardest.

11:49.875 --> 11:51.168
I did it for Do-yeong.

11:51.919 --> 11:52.920
Yes, of course.

11:54.380 --> 11:55.715
Hi! Oh!

11:57.174 --> 11:58.092
Ye-sol, honey.

11:58.592 --> 12:00.010
Say "Grandma" for me.

12:00.511 --> 12:01.929
Say "Grandma."

12:02.930 --> 12:08.561
I will make sure Ye-sol never
<has to try her hardest for anything.

12:17.611 --> 12:18.863
[phone chimes]

12:18.946 --> 12:19.947
[line ringing]

12:22.158 --> 12:24.493
Hey, how has my favorite principal been?

12:24.577 --> 12:26.746
[laughs] If you're free, can I see you?

12:27.872 --> 12:28.789
Yeah, now works.

12:29.290 --> 12:30.916
The homeroom teacher?

12:31.417 --> 12:33.961
The school's chairman
recommended her to us.

12:34.462 --> 12:37.047
Actually, the school was
in a bit of a tight spot,

12:37.131 --> 12:38.382
since Mr. Yang quit so suddenly.

12:38.466 --> 12:39.550
I'm sorry, hold on.

12:40.217 --> 12:43.596
So you're telling me that Dong-eun
personally knows the chairman?

12:44.388 --> 12:45.598
-How does she?
-Uh…

12:46.640 --> 12:47.975
I'm not too sure.

12:48.809 --> 12:51.896
Okay, so is she
even qualified for the job?

12:51.979 --> 12:52.897
Oh, no, no.

12:52.980 --> 12:55.816
We made sure to do our own research,
and her CV is great.

12:56.400 --> 12:57.234
It's odd though.

12:57.318 --> 13:00.112
It's rare for teachers to transfer
from public to private schools.

13:00.196 --> 13:01.572
Ah. I see.

13:03.532 --> 13:06.202
Could I possibly
take a peek at her resume, then?

13:07.036 --> 13:11.916
Ah, well, we have to be careful
with private information nowadays.

13:12.500 --> 13:14.710
Ah. Of course. I know I can't ask that.

13:15.878 --> 13:19.089
So you could just happen to be
holding her resume right now,

13:19.965 --> 13:21.592
and I could just steal a glance.

13:22.468 --> 13:23.469
How's that sound?

13:30.643 --> 13:33.062
[child] Hey! You're doing it wrong!

13:34.980 --> 13:37.107
You can't color it like that!

13:47.243 --> 13:49.578
[suspenseful music playing]

13:56.919 --> 13:57.753
Hey, Ms. Moon!

13:57.837 --> 14:00.464
You're supposed to color
cherry blossoms pink, right?

14:00.548 --> 14:01.924
She's doing it wrong!

14:02.007 --> 14:03.801
I can color them however I want.

14:03.884 --> 14:06.428
Cherry blossoms can be see-through.

14:06.512 --> 14:08.347
[child] You can't do it like that!

14:08.430 --> 14:11.767
Ms. Moon, her drawing is all wrong, right?

14:13.477 --> 14:14.478
[Dong-eun] Hmm.

14:15.312 --> 14:18.023
Seung-a's tulips are full of color,

14:18.524 --> 14:22.278
but Ye-sol's colorless cherry blossoms
are still pretty.

14:22.778 --> 14:24.572
Both are incredible.

14:28.450 --> 14:29.910
[music intensifies]

14:38.043 --> 14:40.212
Why don't we all
try to finish our drawings?

14:41.088 --> 14:42.548
[chilling music builds]

14:58.564 --> 14:59.565
[music trails off]

15:03.402 --> 15:04.403
How much?

15:05.863 --> 15:07.364
Stop playing around now.

15:08.616 --> 15:09.491
I can give it to you.

15:11.076 --> 15:13.162
So just ask for whatever you want.

15:14.455 --> 15:16.832
I promise I'll pay you
for damages, all right?

15:17.791 --> 15:18.834
Mental and physical.

15:20.294 --> 15:21.962
You've just made a lot of money.

15:29.011 --> 15:30.262
Guess we'll sign something.

15:30.346 --> 15:34.099
"Until I die,
you will never see my face ever again."

15:34.767 --> 15:36.852
I'll need that in writing
with your signature.

15:36.936 --> 15:41.732
Like how your mom
signed your high school withdrawal letter.

15:42.566 --> 15:46.153
For people like you, it's usually
their parents who destroy their lives.

15:46.236 --> 15:48.030
You're angry at the wrong person.

15:48.530 --> 15:51.325
Don't try to act tough.
Just tell me how much.

15:51.825 --> 15:52.910
No, wait.

15:53.994 --> 15:57.581
You're not doing this because you want
a sincere apology, are you?

15:58.374 --> 16:01.418
I mean, we're almost 40.
That's only happens in fairy tales.

16:01.502 --> 16:02.670
That's all history now!

16:04.046 --> 16:06.715
What do you want me
to do about it now? Really?

16:06.799 --> 16:08.801
[suspenseful, mysterious music playing]

16:10.302 --> 16:11.303
Of course, I don't.

16:12.513 --> 16:13.514
Don't say sorry.

16:14.348 --> 16:18.352
I didn't bet all of my teens,
twenties, and thirties for an apology.

16:18.435 --> 16:20.187
You deserve to be punished.

16:21.271 --> 16:23.357
If God's on your side, it's what you owe.

16:23.440 --> 16:25.275
If not, you'll know God's fury.

16:25.359 --> 16:26.568
God? [scoffs]

16:27.861 --> 16:30.030
So we're in the scripture,
not a fairy tale?

16:31.156 --> 16:32.157
What God?

16:33.242 --> 16:34.159
Not mine.

16:35.160 --> 16:37.079
So you're holding my daughter hostage.

16:38.122 --> 16:40.791
And? You think God will help?

16:43.168 --> 16:44.086
Hostage?

16:45.129 --> 16:45.963
Who, me?

16:46.547 --> 16:47.798
Have I done anything?

16:49.008 --> 16:50.884
Has Ye-Sol ever been choked by me?

16:50.968 --> 16:53.554
Have I punched her?
Have I slapped her ever?

16:53.637 --> 16:55.389
Or have I burned her with an iron?

16:56.682 --> 16:58.934
So tell me. What have I done to her?

17:07.651 --> 17:11.155
You know, I've actually tried
to be very supportive of her,

17:11.238 --> 17:14.408
as she lives in a world where she doesn't
know that the rainbow has seven colors…

17:14.491 --> 17:15.325
HA YE-SOL

17:15.409 --> 17:17.703
…or can't even tell when food is ripe.

17:17.786 --> 17:21.457
In my classroom,
things like colors don't matter at all.

17:21.957 --> 17:23.125
And that might be…

17:24.668 --> 17:26.754
not great for the position you're in.

17:27.337 --> 17:28.338
How do you…

17:29.089 --> 17:30.591
[menacing music playing]

17:32.092 --> 17:33.385
How'd you find out?

17:33.469 --> 17:35.345
I won't do anything to her.

17:36.180 --> 17:37.931
I can do things to you, though.

17:38.932 --> 17:41.852
For example, parent-teacher conferences.

17:42.603 --> 17:45.022
And as you know,
the mother's not the only person

17:45.606 --> 17:48.358
who goes to parent-teacher conferences.

17:51.403 --> 17:53.989
[menacing music intensifies]

17:57.618 --> 17:58.869
So, never test me

18:01.080 --> 18:02.790
on how far I'm willing to go,

18:04.166 --> 18:06.668
or how far I can
make you suffer, Yeon-jin.

18:07.920 --> 18:12.132
I want you to slowly wither away,
so you understand how it feels.

18:13.133 --> 18:16.470
Slowly, the two of us will die together.

18:16.553 --> 18:17.554
You get that?

18:19.598 --> 18:21.141
I'm so excited for us.

18:26.814 --> 18:28.816
[music swells, trails off]

18:34.863 --> 18:36.782
That's quite an interesting pair.

18:37.449 --> 18:38.700
Wonder what's up.

18:40.536 --> 18:41.703
Hey, Bixby.

18:42.287 --> 18:43.914
Call "Son of a Bitch" for me.

18:43.997 --> 18:44.832
[phone chimes]

18:45.791 --> 18:47.960
[phone] Calling "Son of a Bitch."

18:49.211 --> 18:50.546
SON OF A BITCH

18:51.296 --> 18:53.882
[operator] The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable.

18:53.966 --> 18:56.635
-[sighs] Shit.
-Please leave a message after the beep…

18:56.718 --> 18:58.595
Has that motherfucker really lost it?

19:03.642 --> 19:06.311
Mr. Jeon, someone dropped off
a package for you.

19:07.896 --> 19:09.398
-To here?
-Yes, sir.

19:09.481 --> 19:10.858
Right here, on the street?

19:13.152 --> 19:14.444
They the Avengers?

19:20.868 --> 19:23.620
HA YE-SOL

19:25.747 --> 19:26.748
What is this?

19:30.627 --> 19:32.337
HA YE-SOL

19:35.299 --> 19:37.467
[Do-yeong] Looks like
my secretary's doing a shitty job.

19:37.551 --> 19:39.011
Outsiders aren't allowed in.

19:39.678 --> 19:41.346
Make a lot of money today?

19:42.931 --> 19:45.767
I like it when you wear your work clothes.

19:45.851 --> 19:48.187
I like it better
than when you wear your full suit.

19:48.854 --> 19:49.938
It's so sexy.

19:52.065 --> 19:54.776
I guess you just put Prada
and Versace out of business.

19:54.860 --> 19:57.362
[chuckles]

19:57.446 --> 20:01.909
Honey, should we send Ye-sol
abroad for school?

20:02.993 --> 20:03.994
What're you saying?

20:05.287 --> 20:07.164
Ye-sol is only six years old.

20:08.207 --> 20:11.627
There are a lot of professional guardians
who can keep an eye on her.

20:14.546 --> 20:18.175
Why all of a sudden?
Is it 'cause you want to go abroad?

20:19.259 --> 20:20.552
No, nothing like that.

20:20.636 --> 20:22.095
Then that's even stranger.

20:23.639 --> 20:26.225
You won't even let the nanny
take her to school without a driver.

20:26.308 --> 20:27.976
Now you want to send her abroad?

20:28.477 --> 20:32.022
Sweetie, I heard you've been
golfing a lot with Chairman Kim, right?

20:32.606 --> 20:36.068
Would you be able to arrange
a meeting for us, just this once?

20:36.151 --> 20:38.862
Uh, Ye-sol got a new homeroom teacher,

20:39.821 --> 20:41.365
and she's insane.

20:41.448 --> 20:42.950
How is she "insane?"

20:43.033 --> 20:45.744
Is it that bad that you need
to involve the chairman?

20:45.827 --> 20:47.996
I'll need to know more
before I can do anything.

20:49.164 --> 20:51.458
[chuckles] Actually, don't worry.

20:51.541 --> 20:54.378
I think I'm just a little
overly tired right now.

20:55.420 --> 20:58.423
Now, I'm off to my mother's before work.
I'll call you later.

21:05.013 --> 21:05.889
[door closes]

21:05.973 --> 21:08.183
[pensive music playing]

21:12.354 --> 21:15.023
Her finances, boyfriends, and any family.

21:15.107 --> 21:17.109
Her friends, coworkers, and anyone else.

21:17.651 --> 21:18.902
Just find out everything.

21:20.028 --> 21:21.113
[woman] Good one!

21:21.738 --> 21:23.657
Your mother broke 90 yesterday.

21:23.740 --> 21:24.574
RÉSUMÉ
MOON DONG-EUN

21:24.658 --> 21:26.159
-[phone ringing]
-Dong-eun. Who is she?

21:26.243 --> 21:27.619
JAE-JUN

21:28.203 --> 21:30.914
That's what I'm asking you right now.
I wanna know everything.

21:30.998 --> 21:33.667
Anything I already know
about her is worthless.

21:35.544 --> 21:37.754
[kettle whistling]

21:50.017 --> 21:52.019
[tense music playing]

21:56.732 --> 21:58.358
[woman] Dissolving tablets?

21:59.818 --> 22:00.986
[Yeo-jeong] Yeah.

22:01.570 --> 22:03.905
You know how
a bunch of bubbles start coming up

22:03.989 --> 22:06.325
when you drop
one of those tablets into water?

22:06.950 --> 22:09.911
I start feeling calmer
when I'm listening to that sound.

22:10.412 --> 22:13.749
And why do you think
that sound helps calm you down?

22:15.917 --> 22:18.920
It kinda sound like ginko leaves,
shaking in the wind.

22:19.004 --> 22:21.757
And maybe raindrops
falling softly on a Go board.

22:22.841 --> 22:26.928
And when I keep listening to it,
I start to feel lonely.

22:30.098 --> 22:31.516
Something like that.

22:32.934 --> 22:35.896
Your body's feeling healthy,
while your heart's feeling lonely.

22:36.730 --> 22:39.358
I think it might do you some good
if you changed up your environment.

22:39.441 --> 22:41.526
Like move somewhere new, go on a trip.

22:41.610 --> 22:43.278
I might consider it. Thank you.

22:44.696 --> 22:46.239
I have patients to see.

22:46.823 --> 22:50.285
You must be a good doctor,
since you're always late for our therapy.

22:51.078 --> 22:53.747
But you get paid hourly.
Wouldn't you want me late?

22:53.830 --> 22:55.040
[therapist chuckles]

22:58.043 --> 23:01.088
[sighs] We'll have to run a CT to be sure.

23:01.713 --> 23:04.591
Since it feels hard,
there's a good chance it's osteoma.

23:04.674 --> 23:08.178
Do I really need surgery?
But I can hardly feel anything at all.

23:08.261 --> 23:12.099
You might not have symptoms now,
but it'll start causing discomfort later.

23:12.182 --> 23:13.016
Ah.

23:13.100 --> 23:16.436
So if I do get surgery,
how long will I stay in the hospital?

23:16.520 --> 23:19.106
I teach elementary school,
so I want to do it during a break.

23:19.189 --> 23:20.273
Mmm, probably a week,

23:20.357 --> 23:22.859
with all the exams
and other possible procedures.

23:24.945 --> 23:26.696
-Did you say you were a teacher?
-Yeah.

23:26.780 --> 23:28.407
[gasps] At what school?

23:28.490 --> 23:29.699
How do you enjoy working there?

23:29.783 --> 23:30.742
I've been watching vlogs

23:30.826 --> 23:33.328
where the teachers are always so busy
taking care of the children,

23:33.412 --> 23:34.371
even during their lunch.

23:34.454 --> 23:36.873
Do you find that the kids
actually listen to you?

23:37.791 --> 23:39.960
[chuckles] Are you also a parent?

23:40.043 --> 23:42.003
[chuckles] Oh, I'm not.

23:42.087 --> 23:46.174
Uh, I'm interested in
what teachers usually do, not the kids.

23:46.258 --> 23:47.092
What?

23:47.634 --> 23:48.635
[faucet running]

23:50.804 --> 23:52.806
[mysterious music playing]

24:15.370 --> 24:22.169
SHANGHAI

24:44.191 --> 24:45.859
You, did you lose some weight?

24:46.526 --> 24:47.611
Yeah, a little.

24:47.694 --> 24:50.906
I thought I told you
that our weights need to match.

24:50.989 --> 24:52.532
Now, it won't look the same!

24:52.616 --> 24:55.368
-You should apologize right now.
-I'm so sorry.

24:58.288 --> 25:00.290
Ugh. Just return it. Next one.

25:00.373 --> 25:01.458
I'll do it right now.

25:04.794 --> 25:07.797
Make sure you bring your weight up
before your next flight.

25:08.381 --> 25:10.759
-[chimes]
-If your weight changes again…

25:10.842 --> 25:12.219
Shit, what's this?

25:13.678 --> 25:14.763
What the fuck?

25:16.097 --> 25:17.849
Did your phone get switched with another?

25:17.933 --> 25:19.601
How the hell would I know?

25:19.684 --> 25:22.854
Call Incheon International!
Hurry and ask if they found a phone.

25:22.938 --> 25:23.772
Okay.

25:24.940 --> 25:25.941
[frustrated groan]

25:26.525 --> 25:28.610
What the fuck is this shit? Ugh!

25:34.074 --> 25:35.075
You got it?

25:42.457 --> 25:45.210
Well, it was all very easy.

25:45.293 --> 25:47.629
Got anything else? Tell me what you need.

25:49.798 --> 25:52.092
You did a great job.
I'll see you next time.

25:52.175 --> 25:54.594
Oh, hold on, just wait. Just one second.

25:55.512 --> 25:57.722
You always act so cold whenever I see you.

25:59.891 --> 26:01.101
Here, try this.

26:01.184 --> 26:04.229
[Hyeon-nam chuckles]
I thought we'd be meeting outside again.

26:04.312 --> 26:06.898
Last time, I liked that
it was kinda like a picnic.

26:08.066 --> 26:12.862
This is meant to be very meaningful.

26:14.155 --> 26:16.408
The bird fights its way out of the egg.

26:17.158 --> 26:19.202
The egg is the whole world.

26:19.869 --> 26:20.745
Raemian.

26:21.413 --> 26:23.248
Seon-a was reading their work.

26:24.708 --> 26:26.626
That bird can't fight its way out.

26:26.710 --> 26:27.919
You've gone and boiled it.

26:28.420 --> 26:31.506
Also, Raemian is an apartment.
The book is called Demian.

26:31.590 --> 26:33.592
[rimshot]

26:35.093 --> 26:37.512
It didn't boil. I baked it in the oven.

26:37.596 --> 26:41.349
Am I not allowed to get a little…
Just, like, a little emotional here?

26:42.183 --> 26:43.935
[jazzy, quirky music playing]

26:44.811 --> 26:47.564
Ow! I had a bruise there!

26:47.647 --> 26:49.649
[Hyeon-nam moaning]

26:50.817 --> 26:52.569
It's gonna bruise again.

26:55.113 --> 26:56.406
[Sa-ra's father] My dear beloved…

26:56.990 --> 26:59.034
never seek revenge yourselves,

26:59.534 --> 27:01.286
but leave it to God's wrath.

27:01.995 --> 27:05.999
"Vengeance is mine
and I will repay," says the Lord.

27:06.082 --> 27:07.375
[congregation] Amen.

27:07.459 --> 27:13.423
Let us pray together as we remember
the Lord's own words from Romans 12:19.

27:13.506 --> 27:14.507
Let us pray.

27:16.009 --> 27:19.095
Beloved Father, we truly adore you.

27:19.763 --> 27:23.016
You always embrace us with love,
though we are not deserving.

27:23.099 --> 27:25.602
Allow us to thank you
again for this moment.

27:26.102 --> 27:29.981
Our Lord has always told us
to love our enemies.

27:30.482 --> 27:35.195
But how many times have we tried
to really love and help our enemies?

27:35.695 --> 27:39.908
We have failed to live by your word
and have held grudges against them.

27:40.408 --> 27:42.827
We pray now that you will forgive us.

27:45.747 --> 27:46.665
[Sa-ra sighs]

27:46.748 --> 27:49.918
What's a shitty person like you
doing in a holy place like this?

27:51.002 --> 27:54.673
Sa-ra, I'm genuinely curious,
so let me ask you.

27:55.548 --> 27:58.510
Do you… you honestly believe in God?

27:59.511 --> 28:00.345
Seriously, you?

28:01.137 --> 28:04.307
What you just said… Blasphemy.

28:04.391 --> 28:07.060
Repent. Or you'll suffer God's wrath.

28:07.811 --> 28:09.187
-Oh, yeah?
-Mm-hmm.

28:11.981 --> 28:13.108
[tense music playing]

28:15.610 --> 28:19.364
Mmm. I just happened to pray
and made a pact with God.

28:20.198 --> 28:21.116
He's okay with it.

28:22.409 --> 28:24.703
You're crossing the line, you bitch.

28:25.203 --> 28:27.789
You don't give a shit
about anything as an adult?

28:27.872 --> 28:29.249
Don't do that in here.

28:29.874 --> 28:32.043
Don't use that language in a house of God.

28:32.544 --> 28:33.545
Just hang on.

28:37.507 --> 28:39.134
[exhales heavily]

28:39.217 --> 28:40.051
That's not good.

28:44.264 --> 28:46.015
Your God is super pissed right now.

28:48.101 --> 28:49.686
He says you're going to Hell.

28:49.769 --> 28:50.770
Hey!

28:51.938 --> 28:53.690
Have you lost your shit? Are you on drugs?

28:53.773 --> 28:55.608
You're the one on drugs here.

28:56.109 --> 28:57.444
Pretty often, no?

28:57.527 --> 28:58.570
That's you.

28:58.653 --> 28:59.863
[tense music continuing]

29:01.072 --> 29:02.532
What're you talking about?

29:05.702 --> 29:06.828
You have 15 days.

29:07.328 --> 29:10.373
Fill that with cash and wait
for my message. I want them in dollars.

29:10.457 --> 29:11.291
Hey!

29:11.875 --> 29:14.085
Making a threat like that
is against the law.

29:14.669 --> 29:17.756
Do you have a clue,
how many police officers go here?

29:17.839 --> 29:19.799
You've never been bullied, have you?

29:20.383 --> 29:22.469
Ah! Stop! Let me go!

29:23.386 --> 29:25.388
[dark, menacing music playing]

29:29.601 --> 29:30.435
Ah, shit!

29:30.518 --> 29:35.732
I haven't even started
with you yet, Sa-ra.

29:35.815 --> 29:36.900
[sighs, exhales]

29:39.068 --> 29:39.986
[music fades away]

29:44.115 --> 29:45.408
[GPS chimes]

29:45.492 --> 29:49.078
[GPS] Turn left at the intersection
at University of Education Park.

29:50.622 --> 29:53.374
GYODAE PARK

30:28.743 --> 30:30.161
YEO-JEONG

30:30.995 --> 30:32.372
[Yeo-Jeong] Did you save my number?

30:32.455 --> 30:34.999
Well, I'll make it easy
for you in case you didn't.

30:35.667 --> 30:37.418
Also, this is Yeo-jeong.

30:37.502 --> 30:39.504
[wistful music playing]

30:47.470 --> 30:49.138
There's supposed to be a heat wave today.

30:49.222 --> 30:50.098
How're you doing?

30:50.598 --> 30:52.225
It's supposed to snow a lot today.

30:52.308 --> 30:54.519
Make sure to be careful so you don't fall.

30:55.019 --> 30:56.104
Stay safe.

30:56.187 --> 30:58.940
Did you see the sky today?
It's crystal clear.

30:59.440 --> 31:01.776
I hope you're doing well
and staying healthy.

31:12.328 --> 31:13.663
CIALIS

31:16.374 --> 31:17.375
[Yeo-jeong sighs]

31:22.714 --> 31:25.049
TO: SEOUL JOO GENERAL HOSPITAL
JOO YEO-JEONG

31:25.133 --> 31:26.259
FROM: KANG YEONG-CHEON

31:26.342 --> 31:27.594
[phone chimes]

31:31.389 --> 31:33.308
Yeo-jeong, you got a text.

31:40.315 --> 31:41.566
DONG! EUN! SENT A MESSAGE

31:42.609 --> 31:44.903
-Whoa! Whoa!
-What the… Shit!

31:44.986 --> 31:47.322
I think there's something wrong
with my phone. Look at it.

31:47.405 --> 31:49.782
There's no way she responded
after this long.

31:49.866 --> 31:51.951
I guess we ran into each other that once,

31:52.035 --> 31:53.536
but… but still, she responded?

31:54.454 --> 31:56.205
Maybe she think I looked cool.

31:57.415 --> 32:00.168
Oh, that's it. I get it now. I did.

32:01.210 --> 32:02.795
[friend] Is Dong-eun married?

32:02.879 --> 32:04.380
Don't go reading my texts!

32:06.716 --> 32:08.092
Why? What'd she say now?

32:08.176 --> 32:12.055
Uh, is… is it a wedding invite?
She's getting married? To who?

32:12.639 --> 32:14.474
Ah! It's a divorce!

32:15.266 --> 32:16.100
Or remarrying?

32:16.184 --> 32:17.268
Is she remarrying?

32:18.478 --> 32:20.813
She's asking if you know what Cialis is.

32:23.441 --> 32:25.234
[Dong-eun] Do you know
what medicine this is?

32:25.318 --> 32:26.319
DONG! EUN!

32:27.779 --> 32:29.155
[line ringing]

32:30.698 --> 32:31.616
[line clicks]

32:31.699 --> 32:34.243
-Hey, let's meet up. Where you now?
-[friend] You insane?

32:34.327 --> 32:37.372
-The attending will be here soon.
-Ah, not right now.

32:37.455 --> 32:39.207
Where will you be after 7:00?

33:05.733 --> 33:07.735
Sorry to bug you when you're this busy.

33:07.819 --> 33:11.030
I only got busy after your text.
Had to change my on-call.

33:15.201 --> 33:17.203
[gentle music playing]

33:17.829 --> 33:19.414
Have you still been playing Go?

33:20.832 --> 33:22.917
I play for money sometimes.

33:24.085 --> 33:25.086
[chuckles]

33:27.005 --> 33:29.757
Living in Seoul still?
Or are you in Semyeong now?

33:31.050 --> 33:32.552
How did you know that?

33:33.136 --> 33:35.888
Back then you said
you weren't living there "just yet."

33:37.682 --> 33:39.350
[wistful, romantic music playing]

33:39.434 --> 33:40.518
Moved, right?

33:41.728 --> 33:43.563
Semyeong Elementary is where I work now.

33:47.942 --> 33:50.111
So are you close to that person?

33:50.194 --> 33:52.655
-The one with the medicine.
-No, I'm not yet.

33:52.739 --> 33:55.491
[chuckles] So I guess
they're also a "not yet," huh?

33:59.620 --> 34:02.040
Listen closely.
I'm only gonna say this once.

34:02.623 --> 34:05.376
Cialis is a drug that's based on
something called Tadalafil.

34:05.460 --> 34:07.211
It's got long-lasting effects.

34:07.295 --> 34:08.129
Anything else?

34:08.212 --> 34:12.050
I guess that's good.
This is a product like Viagra, as well.

34:12.133 --> 34:13.468
I know that already.

34:14.469 --> 34:18.389
Could the drug be used for maybe
another purpose other than that?

34:19.599 --> 34:21.934
What kind of other purpose
would you be talking about?

34:23.019 --> 34:25.313
Could it be used
for a different condition?

34:25.897 --> 34:29.776
From what I've heard, some people try it
to cure altitude sickness.

34:31.069 --> 34:32.528
But from a doctor's opinion,

34:32.612 --> 34:34.989
the medication is
for erectile dysfunction only.

34:36.616 --> 34:38.326
Does that man also live in Semyeong?

34:38.409 --> 34:40.036
No. That's not why I asked.

34:40.119 --> 34:42.038
You should meet a guy
that doesn't need that.

34:42.538 --> 34:46.834
As a doctor, I'm a bit concerned.
But you know, as a man, it makes me think.

34:49.003 --> 34:50.505
[sighs] You've got it wrong.

34:53.841 --> 34:57.261
Mmm. Since I last saw you,
you've gotten ruder.

34:57.345 --> 34:59.430
'Cause you're losing
the argument, I'm wrong?

35:05.186 --> 35:06.562
Did you not know

35:07.897 --> 35:09.649
that it was an excuse to see you?

35:12.110 --> 35:13.111
[chuckles]

35:13.194 --> 35:14.195
Yeah. I know that.

35:16.030 --> 35:19.283
You didn't need me when you could've
just looked up what Cialis was for.

35:19.367 --> 35:23.287
But I… didn't know
why you would need an excuse for that.

35:24.372 --> 35:25.540
Got a little too excited.

35:27.291 --> 35:28.960
And although I don't know who he is,

35:29.043 --> 35:31.546
I wonder if this guy has
anything else wrong.

35:31.629 --> 35:34.257
I really hope there's not a single inch
of his body that's healthy.

35:36.676 --> 35:38.427
Just what I thought. Hmm.

35:47.019 --> 35:48.771
I wanted to apologize to you.

35:50.523 --> 35:51.858
What? Apologize?

35:53.151 --> 35:56.028
You see, I don't exactly know
when it happened,

35:57.572 --> 36:01.117
but I was… rude to you.

36:02.785 --> 36:05.454
I'm really sorry if I hurt you.

36:17.091 --> 36:18.092
So, hey,

36:19.093 --> 36:20.428
why does your apology

36:21.596 --> 36:23.347
sound just like a farewell?

36:33.024 --> 36:34.025
This is goodbye.

36:36.068 --> 36:37.904
Gonna tell me to stop texting?

36:40.865 --> 36:42.074
So then why? Huh?

36:42.700 --> 36:45.703
You never respond to me anyways.
You're not interested a little bit?

36:46.370 --> 36:47.371
Fine, then. I'm not.

36:48.706 --> 36:49.790
You're not my type.

36:49.874 --> 36:51.500
Hey, enough now.

36:59.383 --> 37:00.968
I don't know what's going on,

37:02.470 --> 37:05.097
but I don't understand
why you're acting this way.

37:06.390 --> 37:07.225
Right now,

37:08.517 --> 37:10.519
whatever you want to do, just go for it.

37:12.104 --> 37:15.274
But you can date me too.
I know I'll make you happy.

37:17.777 --> 37:19.779
[gentle pop ballad playing]

37:22.240 --> 37:23.950
[Dong-eun] You know those moments?

37:24.659 --> 37:28.412
Those moment in which
you're allowed to like someone.

37:29.622 --> 37:31.999
If moments like those mean you're alive,

37:33.292 --> 37:38.464
then how many days
have I truly lived, Yeon-jin?

37:38.547 --> 37:41.550
♪ Still one thing puzzles me… ♪

37:41.634 --> 37:44.762
Dong-eun, what's so funny?

37:46.514 --> 37:48.224
Guess I'm feeling happy.

37:48.307 --> 37:53.896
♪ Why can't I live a normal life? ♪

37:56.482 --> 37:57.733
But, Yeo-jeong…

37:59.860 --> 38:02.530
I'm not looking for a prince now.

38:04.573 --> 38:06.117
Rather than a prince,

38:07.743 --> 38:12.415
I need an executioner with me,
who can help me in the hunt.

38:13.416 --> 38:17.920
♪ Pain taught me how to live again ♪

38:18.004 --> 38:20.006
[choking]

38:22.341 --> 38:25.136
[whimpers, coughs]

38:25.219 --> 38:29.557
Hang on. They said you'd pass out
after eight seconds. That can't be right.

38:30.057 --> 38:32.977
Come on, she'll pass out
if you hit her hard enough.

38:33.060 --> 38:35.313
If she doesn't, that just means
you're weak as shit.

38:35.396 --> 38:39.483
[Myeong-o] Come on, hey. Who here got
the high score on the punching machine?

38:39.984 --> 38:42.320
-[phone beeps]
-[Myeong-o] That was all me.

38:44.488 --> 38:47.325
[Sa-ra] Dong-eun, tell me if it hurts.
I'll pray for you.

38:47.408 --> 38:48.784
Look here. Come on.

38:48.868 --> 38:51.162
[Myeong-o] Stand straight.
Let's go, Dong-eun.

38:51.662 --> 38:54.540
If I miss, I might hit your boob. [laughs]

38:56.334 --> 38:57.335
[blow landing]

39:10.181 --> 39:11.182
[ballad trails off]

39:19.982 --> 39:24.236
You wanted to talk about
something important at a tteokbokki place,

39:24.320 --> 39:25.905
and you haven't ordered anything yet?

39:28.366 --> 39:31.535
Hey, miss, one tteokbokki
and soondae, please.

39:31.619 --> 39:32.453
[woman] Coming.

39:34.455 --> 39:35.581
You eat soondae, right?

39:36.207 --> 39:37.458
You don't cover your tattoo now?

39:37.541 --> 39:40.127
Tattoo? Ah, this one.

39:41.003 --> 39:42.755
No one gives me shit about it now.

39:43.339 --> 39:45.800
You remember we were
in the same Spanish class, right?

39:46.300 --> 39:48.135
I really hated that class, at first.

39:48.761 --> 39:52.264
But then I started liking it again
because of your tattoo.

39:52.348 --> 39:55.393
Wow. You're dumber
than I would've guessed.

39:56.477 --> 39:58.396
This isn't in Spanish. It's in Latin.

39:59.355 --> 40:00.439
Memento mori.

40:01.107 --> 40:02.691
"Remember that you must die."

40:02.775 --> 40:05.736
Well, you used to
only cover up part of it,

40:06.445 --> 40:08.322
and that meant something else in Spanish.

40:08.906 --> 40:09.782
Mean what?

40:13.202 --> 40:14.995
[trays clattering]

40:17.498 --> 40:18.833
I do eat soondae.

40:20.334 --> 40:21.335
You went to the hospital?

40:22.002 --> 40:22.837
Uh-huh.

40:27.341 --> 40:29.927
Yeah… Looks like you've got something.

40:31.554 --> 40:33.472
So-hee's body was really there.

40:34.098 --> 40:37.852
Yeah. Damn. I don't even know
what the payout would be.

40:37.935 --> 40:41.939
So, who did it?
How much we get will depend on who did it.

40:42.815 --> 40:45.025
-And if I tell you?
-Just say who did it.

40:46.485 --> 40:47.486
Everything else is easy.

40:48.404 --> 40:50.322
I'll grill them about it, day and night.

40:50.406 --> 40:52.241
Make their lives impossible.

40:52.324 --> 40:57.872
I'll turn them all into a huge mess,
then I'll deliver them straight to you.

40:57.955 --> 41:00.332
[suspenseful music playing]

41:00.416 --> 41:02.626
Okay, so there are four.

41:02.710 --> 41:03.711
Who was it?

41:05.713 --> 41:08.382
Was is Sa-ra? While she was high on drugs?

41:10.134 --> 41:10.968
Or maybe Yeon-jin?

41:12.052 --> 41:13.888
She's the scariest out of them.

41:14.638 --> 41:15.639
Or Hye-jeong?

41:16.140 --> 41:19.685
If So-hee spread the rumor
about Hye-jeong and the gym teacher…

41:20.561 --> 41:21.854
Jae-jun?

41:21.937 --> 41:24.064
Maybe So-hui said something
about his eyes.

41:25.608 --> 41:27.610
But now we're together in the same boat.

41:28.235 --> 41:31.155
Which one of those four killed So-hui?

41:40.080 --> 41:41.665
[whispers inaudibly]

41:44.627 --> 41:47.421
Dong-eun demanded you give her money?
How much she want?

41:47.505 --> 41:50.341
Don't know. She threw a bag
at me and said to fill it up.

41:50.424 --> 41:52.843
Fuck, that bag is so fucking big! Shit…

41:53.928 --> 41:56.347
-Why didn't you answer your phone?
-When'd you call me?

41:56.430 --> 41:59.099
-Not talking to you.
-So, then you…

41:59.183 --> 42:01.018
Did she not talk to either of you?

42:01.101 --> 42:02.603
It's not money she's after.

42:03.270 --> 42:05.314
I tried to bribe her,
but she didn't want any of it.

42:05.397 --> 42:08.651
Why isn't Myeong-o answering my calls?
You fired him?

42:08.734 --> 42:10.569
He probably doesn't even know
that he got fired.

42:10.653 --> 42:12.780
He's not answering me. Neither will she.

42:12.863 --> 42:16.659
Do you remember what happened
in high school? Anything?

42:16.742 --> 42:19.662
How's Ye-sol doing?
Since you're here, who's watching her?

42:19.745 --> 42:21.872
What did we even do to Dong-eun back then?

42:23.457 --> 42:24.291
Don't know.

42:24.375 --> 42:26.168
She seriously didn't
throw a bag at you two?

42:26.835 --> 42:29.713
Fuck. She watches way too many movies.

42:29.797 --> 42:31.590
Fill it up with dollar bills?! Fuck me.

42:31.674 --> 42:33.676
Ye-sol must be
in elementary school by now.

42:33.759 --> 42:35.594
Where at? Semyeong Elementary?

42:35.678 --> 42:39.765
What is she going to do to us
to make us suffer like her?

42:39.848 --> 42:43.561
I never even got Ye-sol a gift.
Which classroom is she in?

42:43.644 --> 42:45.646
[suspenseful, dramatic music playing]

43:03.205 --> 43:06.625
Can you please tell me your destination
and if you'd like a one-way or round trip?

43:06.709 --> 43:09.086
Wow. I've always wanted to try this.

43:10.504 --> 43:13.090
And now, finally, I can.

43:18.262 --> 43:20.347
Vladivostok, one-way.

43:21.140 --> 43:25.436
I have been thinking about you
non-stop, all day long.

43:25.519 --> 43:27.146
Wanna meet up later?

43:28.272 --> 43:29.607
Come on, now. Fuck off.

43:29.690 --> 43:32.192
You wanna see me alone? Why?

43:32.276 --> 43:35.154
Now, I'm curious.
Why do you want to see me?

43:35.237 --> 43:37.323
Who's this? Son Myeong-o?

43:37.406 --> 43:39.491
Motherfucker, where the hell are you?

43:39.575 --> 43:42.077
And Yeon-jin? Set a date with her?

43:42.578 --> 43:44.079
[music trails off]

43:48.459 --> 43:49.918
[blow echoing]

44:03.349 --> 44:04.308
[Dong-eun] Me…

44:05.809 --> 44:06.644
"I…"

44:12.149 --> 44:13.067
Mori.

44:17.821 --> 44:18.864
"…am dead."

44:26.997 --> 44:28.999
[moody Korean pop song playing]
